; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Twisting Polygons
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     polygon, rotation, color, spiral, nested
; SUMMARY:  Draws hexagons that grow and turn a little each time, so their corners trace colored spiral arms.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Forty hexagons share the same center. Each one is a little
;   bigger than the one before and turned 4 degrees further. No
;   spiral is drawn on purpose, yet the corners line up into six
;   curving arms. The colors run through the rainbow from the
;   middle outwards.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change SIDES, the turn (4) or the growth (6) in the
;   last line.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * drawing a polygon around a center point
;   * a hidden spiral appears from small steady changes
;   * mixing a rainbow color from a number with SIN
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use squares (4 sides) or triangles (3 sides).
;   * Turn -4 degrees instead. Which way do the arms curl now?
;   * Use a turn of 0. Where did the spiral go?
; ============================================================

; A regular polygon centered on (0, 0). :r is the distance from the
; center to each corner. We jump to the first corner, then visit the
; others in turn.
to centeredpoly :sides :r :turn
  penup
  setxy :r * sin :turn :r * cos :turn
  pendown
  for [k 1 :sides] [
    localmake "a :turn + 360 * :k / :sides
    setxy :r * sin :a :r * cos :a
  ]
end

; A rainbow color for any number: three waves, a third of a turn apart.
to rainbow :n
  output (list 128 + 127 * sin :n 128 + 127 * sin :n + 120 128 + 127 * sin :n + 240)
end

to twist :sides :count :turn :grow
  for [i 1 :count] [
    setpencolor rainbow :i * 9
    centeredpoly :sides :grow * :i :turn * :i
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [15 15 25]
setpensize 2
twist 6 45 4 6.2
